 #uuid "10c6d9fe-4c2a-5584-b952-8a2869149fea" :question/math-academy-id "q-105630" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062906/assets/5e99e02134a5f42aa440cd2d83c971afee3cdb3c210b4488ebccf5cfff1ef8ba.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is defined and continuous on the closed interval $[-3,0].$ By filling the blank spaces in the sentence below, complete the statement of the intermediate value theorem:\n\n*If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{ ________ }$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c\\in [-3,0]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-3,0],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-3)$ and $f(0)$ inclusively.\n\nSince $f(-3)=-1$ and $f(0)=1$, we must have \n$k\\in [-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$-1$ and $1$\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062906/assets/50f937db1a3a87b1887eb22851b285190f1a8999c986af7f1cf32a1676873da2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105630/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d01d143-68f2-534a-8be6-4f63f9ab0d40"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105630"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48430/selection/7d2f68bfc28167237a99533389fc1971a9fdde0f72af7a18e9ac0cc0a7b3e11f" :answer/id #uuid "b3f19b5f-bb77-5c93-8d82-95b55f55caf0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II, I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48430/selection/8cb1ac8c653c3e4210aefd25375265c70521ca375301373600ed4ed37e83b288" :answer/id #uuid "6d43b8c1-c699-5951-80f5-98d285b65b76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III, II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48430/selection/e1b08c30ae6409d86384e6d45f16261c1030a9c86db05f53c8c675e9c30c4980" :answer/id #uuid "fdba5118-c578-5d61-a859-667b43543448" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48430/selection/5aab6e99e2d2fe7023a3e69c393d3f70336151db167624db2d2160c856d46a93" :answer/id #uuid "a3e7a00a-d4ec-585a-9d57-81f945bad7a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II, III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48430/selection/5b0d2458ae733823dd831903d956623078e5a9515cb620d43842b7efd3eee3ad" :answer/id #uuid "2456ac11-e89b-51d6-8093-6004f02adc8a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48430/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a02ee324-a714-50cd-9690-cb1111b82ecb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48430/selection/e1b08c30ae6409d86384e6d45f16261c1030a9c86db05f53c8c675e9c30c4980" :answer-field/choices ["q-48430/selection/7d2f68bfc28167237a99533389fc1971a9fdde0f72af7a18e9ac0cc0a7b3e11f" "q-48430/selection/8cb1ac8c653c3e4210aefd25375265c70521ca375301373600ed4ed37e83b288" "q-48430/selection/e1b08c30ae6409d86384e6d45f16261c1030a9c86db05f53c8c675e9c30c4980" "q-48430/selection/5aab6e99e2d2fe7023a3e69c393d3f70336151db167624db2d2160c856d46a93" "q-48430/selection/5b0d2458ae733823dd831903d956623078e5a9515cb620d43842b7efd3eee3ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48430" :question/id #uuid "78f4f066-a6ea-5590-a2c5-0ffdcc3f7ecb" :question/math-academy-id "q-48430" :question/problem "A statement of the intermediate value theorem is given below but some of its parts are missing.\n\n*Let $f(x)$ be a function that is $\\text{ ______ }$ on a closed interval $[a,b].$ If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{ _________ }$, then there exists a number $c\\in [a,b]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*\n\nGoing from left to right, in which order should the parts I-III, listed below, be placed into the blank spaces to complete the statement of the theorem?\n\n- continuous\n- $f(a)$ and $f(b)$ inclusively\n- defined" :question/worked-solution "The intermediate value theorem states the following.\n\n*Let $f(x)$ be a function that is **continuous** on a closed interval $[a,b].$ If $k$ is a number that lies between $f(a)$ **and** $f(b)$ **inclusively**, then there exists a number $c\\in [a,b]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48430/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d01d143-68f2-534a-8be6-4f63f9ab0d40"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48430"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48429/selection/59a3deeb61083a8594f2c2d383f3182a3e02d63e963f651536ff57d82e1af686" :answer/id #uuid "12d7e2c3-7707-595e-a381-e64804f9a760" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48429/selection/819a757d4e0bc485722090a78c1e2f2785f28af835c17515ba5670f2d7cae63c" :answer/id #uuid "a6dae852-b0c9-5aa8-b216-bf489c47f1b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48429/selection/3087cd408973764228d121a67b15df4a7bae3e55871211934fb2f4c7aad916ca" :answer/id #uuid "09b9fd23-d80c-56fe-800b-92c6175dea1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48429/selection/e39b0820a6ec9909d0527b81b649c9f717eea037a696ad90a8aa2302cb0e8578" :answer/id #uuid "b3bd694c-f78c-5678-8869-a2d5dc564a09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-4$ and $0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48429/selection/85234dcf10779f83197e19789dd7de72d89bfcb132d91a869fec31ef29ae9548" :answer/id #uuid "26149fe6-1006-5add-8412-3f550386c1c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $10$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48429/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4890ae8e-40df-5695-900c-0620b15c647b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48429/selection/85234dcf10779f83197e19789dd7de72d89bfcb132d91a869fec31ef29ae9548" :answer-field/choices ["q-48429/selection/59a3deeb61083a8594f2c2d383f3182a3e02d63e963f651536ff57d82e1af686" "q-48429/selection/819a757d4e0bc485722090a78c1e2f2785f28af835c17515ba5670f2d7cae63c" "q-48429/selection/3087cd408973764228d121a67b15df4a7bae3e55871211934fb2f4c7aad916ca" "q-48429/selection/e39b0820a6ec9909d0527b81b649c9f717eea037a696ad90a8aa2302cb0e8578" "q-48429/selection/85234dcf10779f83197e19789dd7de72d89bfcb132d91a869fec31ef29ae9548"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48429" :question/id #uuid "13761308-9fdd-5204-a133-f89f8f864d21" :question/math-academy-id "q-48429" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}+x$ which is defined and continuous on the closed interval $[1,8].$ By filling the blank spaces in the sentence below, complete the statement of the intermediate value theorem:\n\n*If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{ ________ }$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c\\in [1,8]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[1,8],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(1)$ and $f(8).$\n\nSince $f(1)=2$ and $f(8)=10$, we must have \n$k\\in [2,10].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$2$ and $10$\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-48429/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d01d143-68f2-534a-8be6-4f63f9ab0d40"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48429"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48334/selection/0bcfc91badf3ec9a6c5f1aabe0c5ca6e84e56886e1803ae277c6f306de379e22" :answer/id #uuid "2da35f88-333e-5d07-b9de-9604a067fa9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48334/selection/85cbd7abafd570cda29e9f1798761d7f5b317e8bcfa96dee15d35f65a2d9edde" :answer/id #uuid "92572270-e0a4-5e1e-b48