ider the function $f(x)=8-(x+2)^{2}.$ For which of the following values of $k$ does the intermediate value theorem guarantee that $f(x)=k$ has a solution on the interval $x\\in [-2,1]?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-2,1],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-2)$ and $f(1).$\n\nSince $f(-2)=8$ and $f(1)=-1,$ we must have \n$k\\in [-1,8].$\n\nAmong the given options, only $k=5$ belongs to the interval $[-1,8].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062906/assets/4b9b0cecb305a49f98b7b7a6a2ebca69c1ce10acdb72cb88d805e0f1901dc882.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-78510/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6388d315-340b-56a0-bc93-e380bfbf6ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78510"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47101/selection/14da2cde52e2b4cbd5f8d3cfe2263091da377e92d2867ae7725d0715627ee24a" :answer/id #uuid "a7cbd672-6dbd-5554-a5e7-727e568c1715" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47101/selection/ac9ae2052cc2e067abcad4ecf5a3f3d17a02fa2d9a881931a644b74ccc7546a6" :answer/id #uuid "1d0bf84e-e96e-5a48-bce4-0c9cbdae7676" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47101/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450" :answer/id #uuid "a7267ca4-4925-59fc-8266-e85d1d9604de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47101/selection/b552fda7f0f1aace343d10d4d0d3239e5033799e33a5b6c76d831738f490dc67" :answer/id #uuid "48d33e0a-d0d6-5858-b4eb-8d2c71c47076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47101/selection/a80a330cf07901aff7b5aa904c4a3541c2351751eef1834664dea83e123d76ff" :ans